1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:05,560
Good morning. Welcome to the Early Learning Childcare Centre. How may I help you?

2
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:09,440
Hi. I spoke to you last week about enrolling my daughter for next year.

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:15,690
Oh, yes. I'll just get some details from you. So, you're her mother? That's right.

4
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:19,190
And, can I have your name? It's Carol, Carol Smith.

5
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,260
And your daughter's name? It's Kate.

6
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:25,000
Now, we have several groups at the centre

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,601
and we cater for children from three to five years old.

8
00:00:28,601 --> 00:00:30,270
How old is your daughter?

9
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:33,800
She's three now but she turns four next month.

10
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,770
I'll put four down because that's how old she'll be when she starts.

11
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:41,240
Fine, she's so excited about her birthday and coming to the centre.

12
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:45,380
That's good to hear. And what's your address?

13
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:55,320
It's 46 Wombat Road, that's W-O-M-B-A-T. Woodside 4032.

14
00:00:55,320 --> 00:01:03,330
And what's the phone number? Oh... it's... 3345 9865.

15
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:07,700
So, have you decided on the days you'd like to bring your daughter here?

16
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,960
I'd prefer Monday and Wednesday if possible.

17
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,720
Mmm. I'll check, Monday's fine

18
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:20,530
but I think the centre is already full for Wednesday. Erm. Yes.

19
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:23,080
Sorry. It seems to be a very popular day

20
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,770
We can offer you a Thursday or a Friday as well.

21
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:32,640
Oh dear. I suppose Thursday would be all right because she has swimming on Friday.

22
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,900
OK, got that. Because a lot of parents work

23
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:39,040
we do offer flexible start and finish times.

24
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:43,569
We are open from 7:30 in the morning until 6 o'clock at night.

25
00:01:43,569 --> 00:01:46,480
What time would you like your daughter to start?

26
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:50,900
I need to get to work in the city by 9:00 so I'll drop her off at 8:30.

27
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,220
You're pretty close to the city here

28
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:55,530
so that should give me plenty of time to get there.

29
00:01:55,530 --> 00:02:00,280
That's fine. Now, we also need to decide which group she'll be in.

30
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:04,400
We have two different groups and they're divided up according to age.

31
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:08,360
There's the green group, which is for three to four year olds.

32
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:12,970
And then there's the red group which is for four- to five-year-olds.

33
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:17,480
She's quite mature for her age and she can already write her name and read a little.

34
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,800
Well, I'll put her in the red group

35
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,120
and we can always change her to the green one if there are any problems.

36
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:27,320
That sounds fine. OK. Let's move on to meals

37
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:30,070
We can provide breakfast, lunch and dinner.

38
00:02:30,070 --> 00:02:33,420
As she's finishing pretty early, she won't need dinner

39
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,810
will you give her breakfast before she comes?

40
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:39,940
Yes, she'll only need lunch.

41
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:44,110
Now, does she have any medical conditions we need to know about?

42
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:47,760
Does she have asthma or any hearing problems for example?

43
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:52,550
No. But she does need to wear glasses. Oh, I'll make a note of that.

44
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:56,480
Yes, she's pretty good about wearing them, she can't see much without them.

45
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:01,420
Right. OK. Now, I also need emergency contact details.

46
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,130
So what sort of information do you need?

47
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:10,430
Just the name and number of a friend or family member we can contact in case we can't get hold of you at any time.

48
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:14,960
OK. That'd better be my sister... Jenny Ball

49
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:23,920
That's B-A-double L. Her phone number is 3346 7523.

50
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:28,460
Great. So she is the child's aunt? Yes, that's right.

51
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:33,380
I'll make a note of that as well. Now, is there anything you'd like to ask?

52
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:37,170
What about payment? How much are the fees each term?

53
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:44,400
Well, for two days and the hours you've chosen, that will be $450 altogether.

54
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,470
OK, and do I have to pay that now?

55
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:51,420
No, we send out invoices once the children start at the centre.

56
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:57,160
You can choose to pay at the end of each term or we do offer a slightly discounted rate

57
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,250
if you pay every month.

58
00:03:58,250 --> 00:04:00,020
Oh. I'll do that then

59
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:04,450
I find it easier to budget that way and I'm not used to the term dates just yet.

60
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:07,725
Good, it makes it a lot simpler for us as well.

61
00:04:07,725 --> 00:04:11,000
Well, that's everything. Would you like me to show you around...?
